---
import Wordmark from "../components/Wordmark.astro";
import SessionStrip from "../components/SessionStrip.astro";
import Demo from "../components/Demo.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";

const DOWNLOAD = "https://github.com/gregce/tortie/releases/latest";
const GITHUB = "https://github.com/gregce/tortie";
const DESCRIPTION =
  "Tortie is a macOS shell for coding agents. Sessions run on a private background server that outlives the window, so quitting the app never stops the work.";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Tortie, a macOS shell for coding agents</title>
    <meta name="description" content={DESCRIPTION} />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/tokens.css" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/brand/favicon-32.png" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/brand/favicon-16.png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/brand/apple-touch-icon-180.png" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Tortie" />
    <meta property="og:description" content={DESCRIPTION} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://tortie.sh/" />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://tortie.sh/og.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <!-- The page wears the app's own chrome. Titlebar row, then the band.
         Both are direct children of body so the band can stick to the top. -->
    <header style="display: contents">
      <div class="titlebar">
        <div class="lights" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="light"></span><span class="light"></span><span class="light"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="project-tab">
          <span class="dot dot-working" aria-hidden="true"></span>tortie.sh
        </div>
      </div>
      <nav class="band" aria-label="Site">
        <a href="#top" class="lockup" style="gap: 8px" aria-label="Tortie.sh, back to top">
          <img src="/brand/tortie-mark-64.png" alt="" width="20" height="20" />
          <Wordmark />
        </a>
        <span class="band-spacer"></span>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" href={GITHUB}>View on GitHub</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href={DOWNLOAD}>Download for macOS</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <!-- Hero: the first screen holds the claim and both CTAs. -->
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-inner">
          <div class="lockup">
            <img src="/brand/tortie-mark-256.png" alt="" width="84" height="84" />
            <Wordmark heading />
          </div>
          <p class="hero-line">The sessions were never interrupted.</p>
          <p class="hero-sub">{DESCRIPTION}</p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href={DOWNLOAD}>Download for macOS</a>
            <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={GITHUB}>View on GitHub</a>
          </div>
          <p class="cta-note">Apple silicon. Free under the Apache 2.0 license.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- The proof, directly after the claim. -->
      <Demo />

      <!-- The four pillars, each drawn as a named session. -->
      <SessionStrip name="One window for your projects" id="pillars" />
      <div class="col pillar-body">
        <p>
          Every project is a tab in one window. Switch with <span class="keycap">&#8984;1</span> through
          <span class="keycap">&#8984;9</span>. Everything on screen scopes to the project you are looking
          at. You never search a window switcher for the agent you left working.
        </p>
      </div>

      <SessionStrip name="Durable agent sessions" />
      <div class="col pillar-body">
        <p>
          This is the reason Tortie exists. Sessions run on a private background server, and the app is a
          window onto them. Quit the app and the agents keep working. Reboot your Mac and Tortie restores
          every session with its scrollback. It also arms each agent's own resume command, so one keypress
          continues the conversation where it stopped.
        </p>
      </div>

      <SessionStrip name="Intuitive multiplexing" />
      <div class="col pillar-body">
        <p>
          Sessions have names, and the window is the whole interface. Drag one session onto another to
          split the view. Drop an image from the file tree into an agent. See which session needs your
          input, and jump to it with <span class="keycap">&#8984;J</span>. There are no prefix keys and no
          configuration files.
        </p>
      </div>

      <SessionStrip name="Feels like VS Code" />
      <div class="col pillar-body">
        <p>Tortie keeps the layout you know from VS Code, so there is almost nothing to learn.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A git sidebar that stages changes and shows the history.</li>
          <li>A file tree with git status colors and the icons you are used to.</li>
          <li>Click a file to edit it with Monaco, or diff it against HEAD.</li>
          <li>Project search runs on ripgrep and reaches every open project in the window.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Download -->
      <SessionStrip name="Download" id="download" />
      <div class="col">
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={DOWNLOAD}>Download for macOS</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={GITHUB}>View on GitHub</a>
        </div>
        <p class="cta-note">Apple silicon. Free under the Apache 2.0 license.</p>
        <p class="install-line">
          Drag Tortie into Applications and point it at a project folder. Any folder works. A git
          repository gets the full sidebar.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Refusals -->
      <SessionStrip name="What Tortie refuses to do" id="refusals" />
      <div class="col">
        <ul class="refusals">
          <li>It never touches your own tmux server or your <span class="mono">~/.tmux.conf</span>.</li>
          <li>It never adopts a terminal session it did not create.</li>
          <li>It never previews a key file or anything that looks like a secret.</li>
          <li>It never asks you to watch an agent work.</li>
          <li>It shows no counters and no activity feeds.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="footer">
      <div class="col">
        <span class="lockup" style="gap: 6px">
          <img src="/brand/tortie-mark-64.png" alt="" width="16" height="16" />
          <Wordmark />
        </span>
        <p>Free under the Apache 2.0 license.</p>
        <a href={GITHUB}>View on GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
